Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-20
Subject: Depack `treference' and `tlocation' for the tp2cc C++ bootstrap (fpc 0.99)
License: expat

Same fix as fpc-1.0.6-c-record-packing.patch, applied to the fpc-0.99.14
source tree (where both records live in compiler/cpubase.pas -- the i386
back-end isn't split into its own subdir yet).

These two records carry no file-format role -- they're internal
codegen/operand state for the i386 backend, not written to PPU files or
to disk in any other form.  Upstream declared them `packed' purely to
save RAM on 1990s-era builds.

tp2cc translates Pascal `packed record' to `struct [[gnu::packed]]' in
C++.  Unlike `#pragma pack(push,1)', the attribute form makes GCC flag
latent UB that the pragma silently permits: in particular, binding a
C++ reference to a misaligned packed field (which is exactly what a
Pascal `var' parameter pointing at `treference.offset' or
`tlocation.register' becomes under the C++ lowering).  Those bindings
assume natural alignment for the referent type; the packed-member
address carries no such guarantee, so GCC rejects them with
`cannot bind packed field X to T&'.

On x86 the original FPC code worked because the CPU tolerates
unaligned loads, but under strict C++ rules the resulting references
are UB regardless of hardware.  Depacking these two in-memory records
restores natural alignment without disturbing any on-disk layout, and
lets the [[gnu::packed]] policy keep catching real misalignments
wherever they might appear for records that *are* file formats
(`ppuheader', `tsymbol', `tarhdr' et al., which stay packed).

--- a/compiler/cpubase.pas
+++ b/compiler/cpubase.pas
@@ -425,7 +425,11 @@

   { immediate/reference record }
   preference = ^treference;
-  treference = packed record
+  { was `packed record' -- depacked for the tp2cc C++ bootstrap. This record
+    is in-memory-only (no file-format role), and packing it forced misaligned
+    access to its `longint'/pointer fields. C++ references to those fields
+    are UB when misaligned, which `[[gnu::packed]]' rightly rejects. }
+  treference = record
      is_immediate : boolean; { is this used as reference or immediate }
      segment,
      base,
@@ -477,7 +481,8 @@
   );

   plocation = ^tlocation;
-  tlocation = packed record
+  { depacked for tp2cc bootstrap, see note on `treference' above. }
+  tlocation = record
      case loc : tloc of
         LOC_MEM,LOC_REFERENCE : (reference : treference);
         LOC_FPU : ();
